# Whole worlds that ship on this disk: three unrelated adventure systems, a
# Prolog, and a ray tracer.  Each one has its data here -- which the
# catalogue said of only one of them until these were taken.
shot    infocom
cap     The Infocom Z-machine interpreter running a real story file --
cap     GAMES/INFORM/dejavu.z3, compiled with Inform and shipped here.
run     /dd/CMDS/infocom /dd/GAMES/INFORM/dejavu.z3
wait    8
send    look\r
wait    5

shot    advint
cap     ADVSYS, a second adventure system, playing GAMES/ADVSYS/objects.adi
cap     -- the sample world its author shipped, and the source for it is
cap     here too.
run     /dd/CMDS/GAMES/advint /dd/GAMES/ADVSYS/objects.adi
wait    8
send    look\r
wait    5

shot    adlrun
cap     ADL, a third: Adventure Definition Language, with the AARD world
cap     compiled and ready in /dd/ADL/AARD.
run     /dd/CMDS/ADL/adlrun /dd/ADL/AARD/aard
wait    8
send    look\r
wait    5

shot    sbprolog
for     wam.sbprolog
cap     SB-Prolog 2.2 at its prompt, answering a query.  SIMPATH has to
cap     point at the module library or it exits silently -- which is what
cap     DOC/sbprolog warns about, and it is right.
run     export SIMPATH=/dd/SBPROLOG/MODLIB
wait    2
run     /dd/CMDS/wam.sbprolog /dd/SBPROLOG/MODLIB/\$readloop
wait    10
send    X is 6*7, write(X), nl.\r
wait    6

shot    rayshade
cap     Rayshade 4.0, a full ray tracer, rendering one of its fifteen
cap     example scenes and reporting what it did: primitives, rays cast,
cap     shadow rays, and the time it took.
run     /dd/CMDS/copy /dd/CMDS/GCC139/gcc_cccp /dd/tmp/cccp
wait    5
run     export PATH=/dd/tmp:/dd/CMDS:/dd/CMDS/GAMES:/dd/CMDS/NETPBM:.
wait    2
run     /dd/CMDS/rayshade -R 48 36 -O /dd/tmp/out.pic /dd/GAMES/rayshade/boxball.ray
wait    45
